title: "CrossGen-Forensics: Generalization of AI-Generated Image Detectors Across GAN and Diffusion Models"
abstract: "CrossGen-Forensics is a deep learning forensic framework evaluating the generalization capability of AI-generated image detectors across Generative Adversarial Networks (GANs) and modern Diffusion models (Stable Diffusion 2.1/3/XL, DALL-E 3, Midjourney v6). The system benchmarks unseen-generator generalization, cross-generation transferability (GAN ↔ Diffusion), and 6-class source generator attribution."
date-released: 2026-10-10
url: "https://github.com/m-eshan/CrossGen-Forensics"
repository-code: "https://github.com/m-eshan/CrossGen-Forensics"
keywords:
  - AI Image Detection
  - Deepfake Forensics
  - Generative Adversarial Networks
  - Diffusion Models
  - Transfer Learning
  - Generator Attribution
  - Synthetic Media Forensics
